Scope of this MIT license (apply to Lumenora's own work only)

The MIT text above covers ONLY the original works written by the author for
this repository, i.e. the files this project authors, edits, or assembles as
its own build logic and user configuration. It does NOT grant any license to,
and does NOT relicense, any third-party or upstream software incorporated into
Lumenora's image or installer.

The files covered here are:

  - the BlueBuild recipe definitions: `recipes/recipe.yml`,
    `recipes/recipe-nvidia.yml`, `recipes/recipe-nvidia-open.yml`;
  - the build scripts and configuration under `files/` and `scripts/`,
    including the Lumen Plasma theme (derived artwork and KDE config),
    MangoHud/GameMode/gamescope configuration, skel dotfiles, and the
    GPU-detection tooling under `files/usr/`;
  - the `Containerfile`, `installer/` definitions, and the GitHub Actions
    workflows under `.github/`.
  Each such file, to the extent it is authored by this project rather than
  copied from upstream, is MIT-licensed.

LICENSE applies to the repository's own work only. Regarding the operating
system image this project builds:

Lumenora is an OCI/bootc ("image-mode") build layered on the Fedora Atomic
Desktop (Kinoite) base image at `quay.io/fedora-ostree-desktops/kinoite`
(Fedora release 44). A shipped image is an aggregation of many independent,
individually licensed programs — dozens of upstream rpms, flatpak
applications, firmware, and libraries — plus Lumenora's own small set of
additions. This LICENSE does NOT and cannot relicense those components.
Each keeps its own governing license. The notable examples are listed below
for clarity; the authoritative source for any given package is the license
declared in that package (RPM `License:` metadata, contained `LICENSE`,
`COPYING`, or `LICENSES/` files, and the project's own legal pages). This list
is illustrative, not exhaustive, and is subject to change as packages update.

- Fedora ISO / core operating system packages: there is NO single "Fedora
  license". Every package is individually licensed. GNU core utilities and
  the glibc library are GPL-3.0-or-later and LGPL-2.1-or-later respectively;
  systemd is LGPL-2.1-or-later; each package's own license governs.

- The Linux kernel: GPL-2.0-only (SPDX `GPL-2.0-only`), with the 
  `linux-syscall-note` exception applying to UAPI and syscall-invoking
  userspace. It is explicitly NOT licensed under "GPL v2 or later".

- The Open Gaming Collective (OGC) gaming kernel (which this project swaps in
  via `files/scripts/swap-ogc-kernel.sh`): a fork of the Linux stable tree
  (`gregkh/linux`), i.e. GPL-2.0-only with the same syscall exception.

- KDE Plasma, KDE Frameworks and KDE Gear: primarily LGPL-2.1-or-later, with
  many files also under LGPL-2.1-only, GPL-2.0-only, GPL-2.0-or-later,
  GPL-3.0-only, BSD/MIT, GFDL-1.2 (documentation), and CC-BY-SA-4.0 (media,
  icons). Individual files carry their own SPDX identifiers.

- Qt 6 (on which Plasma depends): LGPL-3.0 or GPL-3.0 for open-source use (not
  LGPL-2.1). The KDE repository enforces its own licensing policy and the
  LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-LGPL/GPL licensing.

- NVIDIA driver stack (in the `-nvidia` image variant only): the NVIDIA
  proprietary graphics driver and CUDA runtime are distributed under the
  NVIDIA/nvidia software LICENSE (end-use license agreement, non-free);
  `nvidia-container-toolkit` is Apache-2.0. The `nvidia-open` kernel source
  flavor (Turing/newer) carries the MIT / NVIDIA license for that hardware.
  These are added by the build's akmods module, belong to their respective
  owners, and are not covered by this file's MIT grant.

- Other bundled tools (gamescope, MangoHud, GameMode, Steam, the `bazaar-store`
  repo packages, oh-my-posh, eza, fastfetch, distrobox, flatpaks) each carry
  their own upstream licenses (MIT, BSD, GPL, LGPL, Apache, Mozilla, CC, etc.).
  Flatpak app runtimes and their dependencies (e.g. the MangoHud Vulkan layer,
  and the freedesktop/GNOME/Qt platform runtimes) carry their own licenses.

Distribution obligations

Redistributing or publishing any Lumenora image, ISO, or derivative triggers
the obligations of each included component, in particular:

- Any GPL-2.0-only / GPL-2.0-or-later / GPL-3.0 code (e.g., the Linux and OGC
  kernels, and any GPL components) must be redistributed in compliance with
  the GPL, including providing complete corresponding source and the license
  text, when redistributed in binary form.
- LGPL components (e.g., glibc, systemd, KDE/Qt libraries) permit dynamic
  linking by this image under LGPL; honor re-linking and documentation
  obligations where applicable.
- Apache-2.0, BSD, MIT, and permissive components require preserving their
  notice files.
- Proprietary components (NVIDIA) remain bound by their own license/EULA and
  must not be redistributed beyond NVIDIA's published terms.

This project follows Fedora's legal guidelines for repackaging and
redistribution. Nothing in the MIT grant above is a claim of ownership or
licensor over any upstream component, and the MIT license text is confined
solely to the files this project itself authors. Distributions, derivative
images, or repackages of Lumenora must themselves comply with the licenses of
all bundled components (including GPL source redistribution).